# Necromancy's 2022-12-08 ruling: which permission it was cast by matters only when it is cast at a time a sorcery couldn't
# have been cast. Bot1 casts it in its own later main phase with an empty stack, beside Valley Floodcaller ("You may cast noncreature
# spells as though they had flash"): it is cast by the rules every player has, so Bot1 is asked no choice of permission, no
# delayed sacrifice is made, and Necromancy (a plain enchantment, with no creature card in any graveyard) is still on the
# battlefield in Bot1's next turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Valley Floodcaller
Sol Ring
Mox Jet
Necromancy
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
